<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa June trade data now due out on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>S.Africa June trade data now due out on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African June trade data had been delayed due to a technical problem and would now be released at 1200 GMT on Tuesday, a Customs and Excise official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The data had been scheduled for release at 1200 GMT on Monday.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast a trade surplus of 1.28 billion rand in June compared with May's 1.75 billion rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
